  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ingesting an object on Windows, managed content datastream, with the datastream defined as follows:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "<foxml:contentLocation REF=\"file:/D:/Fedora34Test/test/datastream.xml\" TYPE=\"URL\"/>",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Ingest fails.  Reports a \"Policy blocked datastream resolution\" error.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "However this is with the deny-unallowed-file-resolution.xml disabled (ie policy deleted; policies reloaded).",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Log with debug turned up is below.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "The error seemingly at the root of this is (the actual error reporting is confusing):",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "(PolicyFinder) An error occured while trying to find a single applicable policy for a request: Malformed object token: file:/D:/Fedora34Test/test/datastream.xml",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "This seems to be coming from org.fcrepo.server.storage.lowlevel.akugra.AkubraLowlevelStorage.getBlobId",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "What is confusing is why the file path ever got through to this class in the first place - I would expect only PIDs or internal datastream identifiers.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Reverting to the legacy storage solves the problem.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Log:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
